//! Native serial mining for admitted Amlogic and AM2 ASIC routes.
//!
//! S19k Pro / BM1366 Track-1 framing is proven independently of its physical
//! UART topology: the held unpacked S19k bosminer has the `55 AA 21 36` rodata
//! prefix at VA `0x12EC448` and its reconstructed packer emits this 88-byte
//! wire frame (see `dcentrald_common::s19k_bosminer_t1_pack` and held live412
//! frame fixtures). Track-1 discovers and admits a multi-UART logical roster;
//! it must not inherit the legacy S19j `/dev/ttyS2`-only claim.
//!
//! Proven S19k Track-1 work packet (88 bytes on wire):
//!   [55 AA] preamble
//!   [21]    header (TYPE_JOB | GROUP_SINGLE | CMD_WRITE)
//!   [36]    length byte (0x36 = 54, bosminer's encoding)
//!   [82 bytes] job payload (BM1366-format: job_id, num_midstates, nonce, nbits, ntime,
//!              merkle_root, prev_block_hash, version)
//!   [2 bytes] CRC-16
//!
//! Legacy S19j Pro / AM2 evidence (not S19k Track-1 topology): bosminer sends
//! work over `/dev/ttyS2`, not FPGA FIFOs; its traced init is a 126-chip route.
//! Its slot-selected I2C addresses are:
//!   0x20/0x21/0x22 = dsPIC voltage controllers (fw byte detected at runtime)
//!   0x51 = EEPROM (hashboard serial/calibration data)
//!
//! Legacy S19j PIC protocol (serialized I2C service writes to 0x21):
//!   Flush: 16x write 0x00 (clear parser state)
//!   GET_VERSION: short [55 AA 17] or framed [55 AA 04 17 00 1B]
//!   ENABLE:      [55 AA 04 15 01 1A] -> voltage on
//!   HEARTBEAT:   [55 AA 04 16 00 1A] -> keep alive
//!   RESET/JUMP bootloader-control opcodes are banned on Pic0x89 paths.
//!
//! AM1 framed-dsPIC boundary (R02, Lead review pending): the Antminer T9+
//! framed dsPIC33EP16GS202 controller (`dcentrald_common::am1_dspic_adapter`)
//! is an FPGA-mediated I²C controller lane, NOT a serial-ASIC route — it must
//! never be composed here. `am1-t9plus` dispatch fails closed in main.rs
//! until a Lead-promoted controller lane exists (CaptureFirst: no unit has
//! ever been contacted; control-board GPIO map and NAND slot layout remain
//! unconfirmed). The S9/S9i/S9j bare PIC16 law (`55 AA 15 01` / `55 AA 16` at
//! 0x55-0x57) likewise rides only the standard BM1387 PIC16 admission, never
//! this module.

